{"title":"Combined feed","url":"https://wulouniu.github.io/feeds/all.xml","elements":[{"title":"Holly Waddington (Wikipedia — did you know?)","contents":"... that for her work in <i><a href=\"/wiki/Poor_Things_(film)\" title=\"Poor Things (film)\">Poor Things</a></i>, the costume designer <b><a href=\"/wiki/Holly_Waddington\" title=\"Holly Waddington\">Holly Waddington</a></b> <i>(pictured)</i> was influenced by the Victorian era, early 20th-century German Expressionism, and 1960s fashion?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holly_Waddington","retrieved":1771653635346},{"title":"Acer wehri (Wikipedia — did you know?)","contents":"... that the fossil maple <i><b><a href=\"/wiki/Acer_wehri\" title=\"Acer wehri\">Acer wehri</a></b></i> is named for a composer, artist, and amateur paleontologist?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acer_wehri","retrieved":1771653635346},{"title":"cut ties with Russia (Wikipedia — did you know?)","contents":"... that Micronesia was the second country to <b><a href=\"/wiki/Federated_States_of_Micronesia%E2%80%93Russia_relations\" title=\"Federated States of Micronesia–Russia relations\">cut ties with Russia</a></b> after the 2022 invasion of Ukraine—the first being Ukraine?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Federated_States_of_Micronesia%E2%80%93Russia_relations","retrieved":1771653635347},{"title":"Times Tables Rock Stars (Wikipedia — did you know?)","contents":"... that <i><b><a href=\"/wiki/Times_Tables_Rock_Stars\" title=\"Times Tables Rock Stars\">Times Tables Rock Stars</a></b></i> added cochlear implants to the game after pupils at a deaf school requested them?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Times_Tables_Rock_Stars","retrieved":1771653635349},{"title":"John Golding (Wikipedia — did you know?)","contents":"... that <b><a href=\"/wiki/John_Golding_(art_historian)\" title=\"John Golding (art historian)\">John Golding</a></b> avoided painting horizontal lines in his work so that his pieces would not be mistaken for landscapes?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Golding_(art_historian)","retrieved":1771653635350},{"title":"New Zealand seafood poster (Wikipedia — did you know?)","contents":"... that the <b><a href=\"/wiki/New_Zealand_seafood_poster\" title=\"New Zealand seafood poster\">New Zealand seafood poster</a></b> is reportedly \"in every fish and chip shop in the country\"?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Zealand_seafood_poster","retrieved":1771653635352},{"title":"Vasyl Khaynas (Wikipedia — did you know?)","contents":"... that historian <b><a href=\"/wiki/Vasyl_Khaynas\" title=\"Vasyl Khaynas\">Vasyl Khaynas</a></b> was active in an underground movement against the Hungarian occupation of Transcarpathia while still in high school?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vasyl_Khaynas","retrieved":1771653635409},{"title":"the medical eye patch (Wikipedia — did you know?)","contents":"... that <b><a href=\"/wiki/Scholz_eye_patch\" title=\"Scholz eye patch\">the medical eye patch</a></b> worn by former German Chancellor Olaf Scholz is said to have increased his popularity?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scholz_eye_patch","retrieved":1771653635409},{"title":"a California TV station (Wikipedia — did you know?)","contents":"... that when <b><a href=\"/wiki/KRCB_(TV)\" title=\"KRCB (TV)\">a California TV station</a></b> began broadcasting, a child sent in 35 cents and a handwritten card reading, \"Now I can get <i><a href=\"/wiki/Sesame_Street\" title=\"Sesame Street\">Sesame Street</a></i><span style=\"padding-left:.15em;\">\"</span>?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/KRCB_(TV)","retrieved":1771653635444},{"title":"Destination of the Month (Wikivoyage recommendations)","contents":"<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r4523569\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\" about=\"#mwt7\" id=\"mwIQ\" data-mw=\"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Banner/styles.css&quot;},&quot;part